WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.175
We've made a couple
of big updates to to-dos

2
00:00:02.175 --> 00:00:04.530
in Basecamp 5, so let's talk about it.

3
00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:07.410
First up is what we're
calling loose to-dos.

4
00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.750
When you wanna quickly jot down a task,

5
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.660
you now have an area
here at the top to do it.

6
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.580
You don't have to first make a to-do list,

7
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.430
you can simply drop in a task.

8
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.350
So just like your other to-dos,

9
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.680
you can give these loose to-dos a deadline

10
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.090
and assign them to people,

11
00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:28.140
but they stay here at the top,
almost like a triage section.

12
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.590
Now, you can still start with
a list first if you wanted to,

13
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.270
but now you have this additional option

14
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.840
to just add a to-do without
having to categorize it.

15
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.750
And when you want to organize
those loose to-dos a bit more,

16
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.530
you can simply drag and
drop them into a list.

17
00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.990
Loose To-dos are not client accessible,

18
00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.310
so you won't see the option

19
00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:50.280
to let the client see them
like you can with a list.

20
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.120
Think of these as just
individual tasks for your team.

21
00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.570
Now the other big update
on to-dos are subtasks.

22
00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:00.690
So when you want to break down
a to-do into smaller steps,

23
00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.190
you can do just that.

24
00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:04.110
So when you add a new to-do,

25
00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.910
or if you click into an existing one,

26
00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:09.120
you'll see this new subtask option

27
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.540
where you can break your
task into smaller steps.

28
00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.040
Those subtasks can be assigned
and given a due date.

29
00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.510
And as those subtasks are completed

30
00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.240
or checked off, you'll
see the little progress

31
00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.380
with the little pie chart.

32
00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.070
And then the last update
on to-dos is a visual one.

33
00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.750
When you check something off,

34
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.900
you'll immediately see a strikethrough.

35
00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.580
And then when you return to the page

36
00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.110
or you refresh that page,

37
00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.500
those completed to-dos
are tucked away nicely.

38
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.690
You can always open those
completed to-dos back

39
00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.250
up if you need to see something.

40
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:48.000
But now the focus is on
what still needs to be done

41
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.760
as opposed to things that
have already been completed.

42
00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.070
So those are the big updates on to-dos.

43
00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.630
As always, if you have
questions, reach out

44
00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:56.970
to our support team at
support@basecamp.com.
